==Trivia==
*Its Japanese name, Kashiwa Mochi 2.0, refers to the traditional Japanese snack [[wikipedia:Kashiwa mochi|kashiwa mochi]] eaten on Children's Day - the basis of the [[Love is Sickness (Monthly Event)|Love is Sickness]] and [[Lovesick Again (Monthly Event)|Lovesick Again]] events.
*Haterbaa 2.0 is the second enemy, alongside [[Metal Doge]], who has a red flickering antenna as a tail to represent the [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] trait.
**In [[Yuru-i GeGeGe no Kitarou: Youkai Dotabata Daisensou|YuruGeGe]], every Metal enemy had one of these antennas on top of their head.
*In Lovesick Again's [[Media:Eve l 017 en.png|event poster]], Haterbaa 2.0 is referred to as "HaterBaa 2.0", with a capital "B", but in later appearances such as [[May Gauntlet II]]'s [[Media:May Gauntlet II Splash.png|event poster]] and the [[Enemy Guide]] entry added in [[Version 13.3 Update|Version 13.3]], the "B" is lowercase.

